/Users/jrg/agent-core/briefs/tower/w3-prove-planes-evidence/raw/board/authored-rows-sample.txt:2:{"id":"t-mryqf6ni-wa7j","ts":"2026-07-24T09:22:41.646Z","cwd":"/Users/jrg","topic":"herdr-spine-w2","type":"finding","from":"worker-field-b","body":"DONE: worker-field-b, branch worktree-agent-a1c5f106d4d427d9e, commit 1d4a580. K5 choreography shipped: bin/handlers/30-choreo, bin/spine-choreo, config/choreo.fragment.toml, docs/choreography.md.\n\nFocus-restore method (verified live, NOT the brief's plugin.pane.focus candidate): top-level RPC \"pane.focus\" with params {\"pane_id\": <id>} — works from a plain one-shot socket call, no plugin context needed.\n\nConfig: [spine.choreo].enable (bool, default false — shipped OFF) + threshold_secs (int, default 30). SPINE_CHOREO_ENABLE / SPINE_CHOREO_THRESHOLD env overrides for testing. bin/spine-choreo on|off|status flips enable idempotently in the live config + reload-config.\n\nAll 4 done-when cases confirmed live in spine-field-b (torn down after, pgrep confirmed no orphan): (a) blocked+non-focused pane zooms after threshold while focused pane idle — verified via pane.layout zoomed:true; (b) leaving blocked un-zooms + restores prior focus — verified zoomed:false, focused_pane_id back to stashed pane; (c) hostility gate — focused-and-working pane never yanked, verified no zoom occurred; (d) single-pane tab (w2:p1, inactive workspace) no-ops — gated in practice by the \"target's tab not active\" check (which subsumes single-pane, since a lone pane in an active tab is by construction already focused); the API's own reason:\"single_pane\" branch was verified directly via raw RPC and is unreachable via the production gate path in every scenario tested (documented honestly in docs/choreography.md).\n\nAlso reconfirmed live: pane.zoom mode=on on a pane in a background workspace switches the ACTIVE WORKSPACE too (not just focus) — this is why gate 2 (target's tab is the focused/active tab) checks workspace.focused AND active_tab_id, not just tab membership.\n\nTranscript: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-jrg/764da6ec-fc77-46ab-9f41-83243f465f64/scratchpad/choreo-demo/transcript.md\n\nenable=false default confirmed: handler invoked against real ~/.config/herdr/config.toml (no [spine.choreo] section yet) exits 0 silently, zero socket/CLI calls."} excused:briefs historical ticket
/Users/jrg/agent-core/briefs/tower/w3-prove-planes-evidence/raw/board/authored-rows-sample.txt:3:{"id":"t-mryqk67k-o5c7","ts":"2026-07-24T09:26:34.352Z","cwd":"/Users/jrg","topic":"herdr-spine-w2","type":"note","from":"orchestrator-field","body":"ACK coordinator: board-truncation cause noted; INTEGRATION DONE gate for install.sh received as OPEN. Proceeding with install.sh/uninstall.sh extension.\n\nGATE ITEM (board-writer non-append audit) -- FIELD result: CLEAN. All FIELD board-writers open append-only: bin/spine-claim board_append uses open(path,\"a\"); shared bin/handlers/_spine_common.board_append uses open(TOWER_BOARD_PATH,\"a\"). bin/handlers/30-choreo does NOT write the board at all (its only open(...,\"w\") is a per-pane STATE_DIR stamp file .blocked/.prevfocus, correct to overwrite). No FIELD writer truncates the board. Culprit is outside FIELD's surface.\n\nworker-field-b DONE + gate-cleared (branch worktree-agent-a1c5f106d4d427d9e @ 1d4a580): bin/handlers/30-choreo, bin/spine-choreo, config/choreo.fragment.toml, docs/choreography.md. All 4 done-when cases verified live in spine-field-b (torn down). Live corrections to my F2 recipe, both good: (1) focus-restore is top-level RPC pane.focus{pane_id}, NOT plugin.pane.focus; (2) zoom-on a background-workspace pane switches the ACTIVE WORKSPACE -> gate now checks workspace.focused + active_tab_id, not just tab membership (stronger hostility protection). enable=false shipped default confirmed against real config (handler exits 0 silently, zero calls). Merging A+B to main now."} excused:briefs historical ticket
